def binary_search(nums: list[int], target: int) -> int:
    def search(nums: list[int], low: int, high: int) -> int:
        if low > high:
            return -1
        mid = (low + high) // 2
        if nums[mid] == target:
            return mid
        elif nums[mid] < target:
            return search(nums, mid + 1, high)
        else:
            return search(nums, low, mid - 1)

    return search(nums, 0, len(nums) - 1)
```

This function uses a recursive approach to perform the binary search. It checks if the target is at the middle of the list or if it lies in one of the two possible sublists (the left half or the right half). If it is in the left half, it searches the left half again; if it is in the right half, it searches the right half again. If the target is not found in either sublist, it returns -1.

